cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, methodology, or published search records, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SETIsearch: Panchromatic (>4-Octave, 0.1145-2.515 um) Space-FUV, Optical, Near-IR Echelle Laser, Frequency-Comb, Radio & Photometric Technosignature Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Prospectively locked, reproducible archival searches and pure-stdlib numerical audits
  for panchromatic space far-UV (HST_STIS E140M, 0.1145-0.1710 um), near-UV (VLT UVES_NUV),
  optical, far-red (VLT UVES_RED, 0.5655-1.0425 um), near-infrared YJH, thermal K-band,
  and simultaneous YJHK laser and periodic frequency-comb technosignatures (0.1145-2.515 um,
  4.457 octaves across 9 spectrographs / 10 arms: HST/STIS, VLT UVES_NUV & UVES_RED,
  ESO HARPS, VLT ESPRESSO HR/UHR, ESO NIRPS, VLT CRIRES+, TNG HARPS-N, Calar Alto
  CARMENES_VIS, CFHT 3.6 m SPIRou APERO 0.7.295, and FEROS; 200 unique stars and 1,391
  high-resolution echelle exposures totaling 335.26 h in V3.0-V3.8 + COMB_V4_1 with
  Keplerian planetary de-Doppler, G4_V38 Fiber-B simultaneous-cal bleed veto (577->0),
  2D CCD/MAMA/H2RG/H4RG vetoes, sparse G6 coincidence gating, and COMB_V4_1 matched
  filtering), unified with planetary-rest-frame 1.4 GHz narrowband radio searches
  (Parkes/GBT) and TESS specular light-sail photometry into a 206-system all-sky
  multi-messenger synthesis (0 verified ETI detections, 0.0973 W FUV limit on Proxima Cen).
authors:
